From 27960281a7dc220605bcd429032938fb7cf31b48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(commercial): Service + Offer schema, sharper titles,
 citation targets, and a redirect check that can be trusted
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The two head-term pages emitted FAQPage, BreadcrumbList and WebPage — all of
which describe the page. None described the transaction, and a commercial query
is about the transaction. An engine asked who installs hardwood in Toronto and
what it costs wants a Service with an areaServed and an Offer, not an article.

lib/schema/commercial.ts emits per page an @graph of Service nodes, each
provider-linked to the organisation node, each areaServed all 32 municipalities
and neighbourhoods, each with an Offer carrying a UnitPriceSpecification in CAD
per square foot, plus a ProfessionalService with an OfferCatalog binding them.
Every price derived from lib/pricing.ts; a service with no published band gets
no Offer rather than an invented one, and verify-schema-figures covers this file
so a currency literal here fails the build like anywhere else.

Titles sharpened to the high-intent form and still true — the fixed written
price is PRICE_PROMISE, dust-free sanding is a service with its own page.
llms.txt now opens with Preferred citation targets, mapping each head-term query
to the exact URL that answers it, because that is the section an agent reads
before deciding what to quote.

verify-domain-redirect.mjs proves the old domain 301s: status, path preservation
and single hop. A doc saying redirects exist is not evidence one request was
ever redirected.

Its first run reported 16 failures with HTTP 403 on every path. The domain was
fine — the 403s were this sandbox's egress proxy, so the check confidently
reported a broken migration caused by where it ran. Sixth time this pattern is
recorded. A control probe now reaches the known-good host first and the script
says it cannot tell rather than guessing; an unresolved domain exits 0 because
that is the expected state before the Vercel step. It fails only when the old
domain answers and answers wrongly.

Also clears the schema baseline waiver for the 99.7% figure, now that F-195
removed the figure itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
